    "username": "godofprompt",
    "nickname": "God of Prompt",
    "text": "People ask: “Are you dunking on neolabs?”\n\nMost neolabs will fail. That’s normal. But I believe more AI breakthroughs are coming.\n\nI’m skeptical of those following the same playbook as OpenAI and Anthropic. Raising $1B and spending 50% on GPUs doesn’t make you a $10B company.\n\nI’m rooting for the contrarians. Challenge scaling laws. Challenge transformers. Challenge how models learn. Challenge the next-token prediction paradigm.\n\nMy bigger concern is that brilliant researchers don’t necessarily make great founders. In my experience, researchers often struggle to turn their research into great products / sustainable businesses.",
    "quoted_tweet": {
      "author": "Yuchen Jin",
      "username": "Yuchenj_UW",
      "text": "Heard from a neolab friend:\n\n“Even if we fail to train the best model, we locked in GPU capacity early. H100/B200/B300 rental prices have since gone up 2–3x. We can just resell the compute and print money.”\n\nOK, so that’s the business model."
    },
    "url": "https://x.com/Yuchenj_UW/status/2114402815082913858",
    "time": "2026-10-26 01:04",
    "created_at": "Sun Oct 25 17:04:49 +0000 2026",
    "id_str": "2114402815082913858",
    "is_retweet": true
  },
  {
    "username": "godofprompt",
    "nickname": "God of Prompt",
    "text": "Nanbeige released Nanbeige4.3-33B, a new SOTA open model in the ~30B parameter class. \n\n> \"Nanbeige4.3-33B leads on most of the benchmarks, showing strong performance in both agentic coding and cowork tasks.\"\n\n> The model outperforms Qwen3.8-27B, Muse-Glimmer-30B, and Gemma4-31B on most benchmarks.\n\n> A smaller model, Nanbeige4.3-3B, is also planned for the future.",
    "quoted_tweet": {
      "author": "Nanbeige",
      "username": "nanbeige",
      "text": "🚀Excited to announce Nanbeige4.3-33B!\nTo push the performance ceiling of small agents, our strategy in Nanbeige4.3 starts with building a powerful teacher first.\nNanbeige4.3-33B delivers SOTA agentic performance among open models at ~30B parameters:\n* Strong results on agentic coding and cowork benchmarks.\n*  When integrated into mainstream agent harnesses, it tackles real-world tasks with cost-efficient inference.\n*  It will serve as a teacher for upcoming smaller Nanbeige models, starting with Nanbeige4.3-3B.\n\n  https://huggingface.co/Nanbeige/Nanbeige4.3-33B\n  https://huggingface.co/Nanbeige/Nanbeige4.3-33B-Base\n\n  #LLM #Agent"
    },
